  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;NƯỚC VIỆT NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nước Việt Nam is the country with a long coastline and diverse interiors, located in Southeast Asia; it has been a cradle for many cultures and a central stage for regional conflicts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam, a country with a long coastline and interior mountains, historically the cradle of many cultures; its strategic location in Southeast Asia has made it a crossroads of trade and a focal point of various conflicts throughout history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam, with a long coastline and interior mountains, is the cradle of many cultures across history; strategically located in Southeast Asia as a crossroads of trade and a focal point of conflicts."(&lt;SEP&gt;"Nước Việt Nam là quốc gia có đường bờ biển dài và vùng interior nhiều dãy núi hiểm trở, là cái nôi của nhiều nền văn hóa và vị trí địa chiến lược ở Đông Nam Á."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">NƯỚC VIỆT NAM&lt;SEP&gt;VIỆT NAM</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐÔNG NAM Á&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""&lt;SEP&gt;"Geographic region receiving diffusion of wet rice farming and migrations from South China."&lt;SEP&gt;"Geographic region where Bronze Age developments occurred; referenced in relation to bronze artifacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southeast Asia region mentioned in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Southeast Asian region that provides the strategic context for Vietnam's historical development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region of Southeast Asia, a key geographic and strategic area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region encompassing continental and maritime Southeast Asia where farming and population movements occurred."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southeast Asia region; Vietnam's location is central to trade routes and regional conflicts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vùng lãnh thổ Đông Nam Á, nơi có liên hệ với các nền văn hóa cổ Việt Nam và Đông Sơn trong thời kỳ đồ đồng và các giai đoạn lịch sử cổ đại."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Southeast Asian region; destination of early agricultural migrations from East Asia; site of diffusion into continental and island Southeast Asia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vùng Đông Nam Á, khu vực nơi Việt Nam nằm và là ngã tư giao thương cũng như địa điểm các cuộc xung đột lịch sử."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df404f664a0d60546a9e31eb5bdff3ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc55d62fe8c98a4db1992322d16a5280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">REGION OF SOUTHEAST ASIA MENTIONED AS THE GEOGRAPHIC CONTEXT FOR MIGRATIONS AND EARLY AGRICULTURE IN THE TEXT.&lt;SEP&gt;ĐÔNG NAM Á</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VĂN LANG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ancient Vietnamese state mentioned alongside Đông Sơn, Âu Lạc and Hồng Bàng; appears in legends such as Thánh Gióng."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state named by the Hùng Vương; its capital was at Phong Châu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state that preceded Âu Lạc, associated with early dynastic development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state, active in the Đông Sơn era and predecessor to Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc hiệu được các vị Hùng Vương đặt ra và là trung tâm quyền lực với đô phủ tại Phong Châu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Văn Lang is an ancient Vietnamese state mentioned among the polities linked to the Đông Sơn cultural sphere, representing early state formation in Vietnamese history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state around the Văn Lang period; precursor to Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc hiệu và nhà nước cổ đại của người Việt, đóng đô tại Phong Châu; được đề cập cùng với Âu Lạc và Hồng Bàng trong thời kỳ này."&lt;SEP&gt;"Văn Lang is an ancient Vietnamese state that scholars commonly associate with the Đông Sơn culture, along with Âu Lạc and Hồng Bàng."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state whose rulers were the Hùng Vương; capital at Phong Châu."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Văn Lang is one of the ancient Vietnamese states mentioned as part of the Đông Sơn cultural milieu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Văn Lang là một trong các vương quốc bản địa trước đây của Việt Nam, đóng vai trò nền tảng cho sự hình thành các nhà nước sau này."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">VĂN LANG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ÂU LẠC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient Vietnamese polity that followed Văn Lang; later defeated as part of regional power shifts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state formed by the merger of Au Viet and Lac Viet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom formed by uniting Âu Việt and Lạc Việt; Thục Phán proclaimed as An Dương Vương; capital later associated with Phong Khê."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state formed after Văn Lang; region later associated with the south."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà nước cổ sau Văn Lang, một phần lịch sử Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Lạc is an ancient Vietnamese state formed in 257 BCE from the merger of Âu Việt and Lạc Việt; it existed until it was annexed by Nam Việt around 179 BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state that followed Văn Lang."&lt;SEP&gt;"Một nhà nước cổ đại trong thời kỳ Văn Lang và Đông Sơn; liên quan tới Hong Bang."&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Lạc is a kingdom formed in 257 BCE by the union of Âu Việt and Lạc Việt; Thục Phán proclaimed himself An Dương Vương and the state is linked to him; later it was conquered by Nam Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese state mentioned alongside Văn Lang and Hồng Bàng within the Đông Sơn cultural context."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Lạc is the kingdom formed by unification of Âu Việt and Lạc Việt; in 257 BCE, Thục Phán proclaimed himself An Dương Vương and a new kingdom Âu Lạc emerged."&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Lạc là một nhà nước cổ tại Việt Nam, sau này bị Triệu Đà diệt và thay thế bằng Nam Việt."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3">0257&lt;SEP&gt;257–179 TCN</data>
      <data key="d4">AU LAC&lt;SEP&gt;ÂU LẠC</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NỀN VĂN HÓA ĐÔNG SƠN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early Vietnamese cultural formation based on wet-rice agriculture, centered around the Văn Lang and Âu Lạc era."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">NỀN VĂN HÓA ĐÔNG SƠN&lt;SEP&gt;VĂN HÓA ĐÔNG SƠN&lt;SEP&gt;ĐÔNG SƠN CULTURE</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIỆU ĐÀ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A former Qin general who established Nam Việt; defeated An Dương Vương in 179 BCE and annexed Âu Lạc into his realm."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ancient ruler of the Nam Việt (Nanyue) kingdom; historical figure mentioned in the text; alias Zhao Tuo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical ruler who diệt (conquered) Âu Lạc around 179 BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"A ruler who established rule in southern Vietnam and is noted for conquering Âu Lạc in 179 BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triệu Đà was a former general of the Qin (Nhà Tần) who established Nam Việt in 207 BCE and later conquered Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient ruler whose kingdom is referred to as Nam Việt; used here to illustrate the historical naming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ruler who defeated Âu Lạc in 179 BCE, founding Nam Việt under Han influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triệu Đà was a former Tsin general who established the Nam Việt kingdom in 207 BCE in the southern coast area (Guangdong/Guangxi today)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient ruler whose kingdom is referenced to explain naming changes; part of historical context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triệu Đà là người đã diệt Âu Lạc và thành lập Nam Việt, khoảng năm 179 TCN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triệu Đà, a former general of the Qin, established the kingdom of Nam Việt in the southern coastal region and later annexed Âu Lạc."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3">0207&lt;SEP&gt;179</data>
      <data key="d4">CHIEU DA&lt;SEP&gt;TRIỆU ĐÀ</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAM VIỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A historical Vietnamese polity/region that was invaded by the Han and later subdivided into Han administrative districts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient southern Vietnamese kingdom; experienced invasion by the Han dynasty around 111 BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient southern Vietnamese region conquered by the Han; subsequently divided into prefectures (Giao Chỉ, Cửu Chân, Nhật Nam)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Vietnam; used in the text to reference the country before modern naming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom established by Triệu Đà along the southern coast of present-day Guangdong and Guangxi; later incorporated into his domain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt is a historical southern Vietnamese region; in this text, Đinh Liễn is titled Nam Việt vương, indicating his royal authority in the Nam Việt realm during the Đinh era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical Vietnamese state in the region around southern Vietnam under Han influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt is a kingdom established in 207 BCE by Triệu Đà; it later defeated An Dương Vương and annexed Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical kingdom; associated with the Nam Việt vương Đinh Liễn mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt is a kingdom founded by Triệu Đà in 207 BCE and expanded to rule Âu Lạc; later Triệu Đà's dynasty asserted independence from Han."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt is the ancient Vietnamese land invaded by the Han and later divided into the prefectures of Giao Chỉ, Cửu Chân, and Nhật Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt was the name proposed to rename Đại Việt by Gia Long; referenced in the discussion of national names."&lt;SEP&gt;"State under Han influence after defeating Âu Lạc (179 BCE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical regnal name proposed for Vietnam after An Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt is the kingdom established by Triệu Đà (the beginning of the Nam Việt/Triệu dynasty period)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Việt là nhà nước dưới sự mở rộng của nhà Hán, chiếm một phần lãnh thổ Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region in southern China/northern Vietnam that was conquered by the Han and thereafter divided into districts (Giao Chỉ, Cửu Chân, Nhật Nam) under Han administration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01995274690fe1835d7836e3a481a678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d</data>
      <data key="d3">0111&lt;SEP&gt;0179&lt;SEP&gt;0207&lt;SEP&gt;179–111 TCN</data>
      <data key="d4">NAM VIET&lt;SEP&gt;NAM VIỆT</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NHÀ HÁN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Han Dynasty; referenced as the historical context preceding Tang reforms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Han dynasty; imperial China that invaded Nam Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Han Dynasty; the text notes Chinese domination in the north during this period."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The Han Dynasty, a Chinese imperial dynasty that invaded Nam Việt and established administrative districts (Giao Chỉ, Cửu Chân, Nhật Nam); Han rulers governed through Thái thú and officials, while local Vietnamese aristocracy retained some power in mountainous areas; Buddhism, Daoism, and Confucianism were introduced to Vietnam during this period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà Hán (Han Dynasty)"&lt;SEP&gt;"The Han Dynasty; referenced in the text within the Bắc thuộc context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà Hán (Han dynasty) is referenced as the northern power contemporaneous with these events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà Hán là đế chế Trung Hoa đã chiếm và thống trị vùng Việt Nam trong thời kỳ BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Han dynasty, a major Chinese imperial power, invaded Nam Việt in 111 BCE and established administrative divisions over the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01995274690fe1835d7836e3a481a678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3">0111</data>
      <data key="d4">HÁN&lt;SEP&gt;HÁN DYNASTY&lt;SEP&gt;NHÀ HÁN</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CỔ ĐÔNG Á&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient East Asia region from which hunter-gatherer groups reached Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient East Asia region referenced as part of broad migration and cultural context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cổ Đông Á chỉ nhóm thợ săn–hái lượm đầu tiên đến Việt Nam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">CỔ ĐÔNG Á</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHĂM PA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""&lt;SEP&gt;""&lt;SEP&gt;"A neighboring kingdom that allied with Mai Thúc Loan during the revolt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa kingdom in central Vietnam region; subject of conflict with Đại Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa kingdom in central Vietnam; subject of conflict with Đại Việt; diaspora after conquests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa; ancient kingdom in present-day central Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa) was a neighboring kingdom involved in conflicts with Đại Cồ Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa is a historical kingdom in present-day central Vietnam; in 1312 it became a vassal of Đại Việt, later waging a long war to regain independence; its capital was Vijaya."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early Champa kingdom in central Vietnam; context for Cham uprisings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical region (Champa) in central Vietnam; referenced in historical contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom in southern-central Vietnam; adversary/ally with Đại Việt; involved in marriage alliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom of Champa; allied with Khmer against Đại Việt during 1128 and 1132 invasions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region/kingdom in central Vietnam; expansion target of Nguyễn dynasties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cham kingdom of Lâm Ấp in central Vietnam; a prosperous, trade-driven polity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Champa kingdom mentioned as a major regional power and adversary in Khmer-Champa conflicts and trade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa Kingdom, historic neighbor interacting with Vietnamese states."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa) was a southern kingdom allied with Khmer and involved in invasions of Đại Việt around 1128 and 1132."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa), an ancient kingdom that engaged in regional trade and conflict with the Khmer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa, a historical kingdom in central Vietnam, became a vassal of Đại Việt in 1312 and later regained independence to wage a prolonged war to reclaim lands during the 14th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom in the south that became a vassal to Đại Việt in 1312."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom of Cham Pa, a prosperous Cham polity also called Lâm Ấp; engage in trade and conflict with Khmer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom of Champa; attacked Đại Cồ Việt under Paramesvararman I."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region of Champa; part of historical Vietnamese frontier."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cham kingdom that emerged from Lâm Ấp; a major cultural and political power in central Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Champa kingdom in central Vietnam, with significant historical interactions with Đại Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Champa kingdom, which faced expansion and conflict with Đại Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa kingdom; historical region mentioned as attacked."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa kingdom; region attacked by Lê Thánh Tông."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa; allied with Khmer Empire in invasions of Đại Việt in 1128 and 1132."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa; historical kingdom allied with Khmer to invade Đại Việt in 1128 and 1132."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa) region in central Vietnam; subject of Nguyễn expansion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa) was a historic kingdom/region in the area of modern central to southern Vietnam; it engaged in maritime trade and clashed with the Khmer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa is the Champa kingdom that became a vassal of Đại Việt in 1312; later regained independence and launched a protracted 30-year war to reclaim lands; participated in campaigns against Đại Việt, including attacks on the capital Thăng Long; the Cham city Vijaya (1377) is noted as the site where Trần Duệ Tông was killed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early Champa kingdom in central Vietnam; later a major cultural, Buddhist and Hindu center in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early Champa kingdom spanning central Vietnam; includes Lâm Ấp, Tây Đồ, Khuất Đô Càn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom of Champa that attacked Đại Cồ Việt under Paramesvaravarman I."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liên minh với Mai Thúc Loan; đồng minh trong khởi nghĩa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cham Pa, the early Cham kingdom; a major cultural and political entity in central Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa (historical region of central Vietnam)"&lt;SEP&gt;"Champa; a southern kingdom that, with Khmer, attacked Đại Việt in the broader imperial contests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa) was a historic polity in the region of central Vietnam; it became a vassal of Đại Việt in 1312 and later mounted a prolonged conflict to regain its lands."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champa) was involved in the conflict with Đại Cồ Việt, as Paramesvararman I attacked the Vietnamese state and Ngô Nhật Khánh sought refuge there."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (Champā) is the Champa kingdom that expanded trade and later came under Khmer influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa (also known as Lâm Ấp) is the ancient Cham kingdom in central-southern Vietnam. It prospered from its strategic position on early trade routes linking the Middle East and China, with capitals such as Simhapura and Indrapura. The kingdom engaged in sustained conflict with the Khmer Empire and experienced periods of expansion, consolidation, and religious-cultural development (Buddhist and Hindu influences) across a long durée (7th–13th centuries)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa là một vương quốc cổ ở miền Trung và Nam Việt Nam, bị ảnh hưởng và tranh chấp bởi các thế lực Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom of Champa, engaged in a marriage alliance with Đại Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom of Champa; invaded by Lê Thánh Tông in 1471."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bc2794dad524831d7084c6c23b70cd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4943e96cb569799b168fc03f9b7f0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1095d21a9a487ebf90afcd96d02737d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fca97c72fe1e0e81ac8addb98deb7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277de9a31fb7056270b32bed48f417c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561d10717f3ff788e1032021a4cf0614</data>
      <data key="d3">0192"&lt;SEP&gt;1128&lt;SEP&gt;1312&lt;SEP&gt;722"&lt;SEP&gt;979</data>
      <data key="d4">""'&lt;SEP&gt;""**&lt;SEP&gt;CHAM PA&lt;SEP&gt;CHAM PA KINGDOM&lt;SEP&gt;CHAMPA&lt;SEP&gt;CHĂM PA&lt;SEP&gt;LÂM ẤP</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TỐNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nhà Tống (Song Dynasty) là đế chế Trung Hoa từng xâm lược và ảnh hưởng đến khu vực Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Song dynasty of China; invasions into Vietnamese territory in historical times.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Song dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Song dynasty, a major adversary in the 1075 campaign."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Song dynasty, opponent of Đại Việt during the 1075 campaign."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Song dynasty; adversary of Đại Việt, which launched a retaliation in 1076 after initial campaigns."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3">1075</data>
      <data key="d4">NHÀ TỐNG&lt;SEP&gt;TỐNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYÊN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nhà Nguyên (Yuan Dynasty) là đế chế Trung Hoa từng có sự can thiệp và xâm lược khu vực Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yuan Dynasty; invasions and conflicts with Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yuan dynasty."</data>
