      <data key="d1">"1407"&lt;|"Ming Dynasty; invaded Đại Ngu in 1407 and occupied/annexed the territory under the Fourth Ming domination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ming dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ming Dynasty; occupying force of Đại Việt during the Lam Sơn uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ming Dynasty of China; invaded Đại Ngu in 1407, captured Hồ Quý Ly and Hồ Hán Thương, and annexed Đại Việt as Giao Chỉ."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ming dynasty of China, whose interactions with Vietnam included invasions and conflicts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ming dynasty; briefly occupied parts of Vietnam in the 15th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ming Dynasty; opponent in the Lam Sơn uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ming dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ming dynasty invaded Đại Ngu in 1407 under the pretext of 'phù Trần diệt Hồ', captured Hồ Quý Ly and Hồ Hán Thương, and absorbed Đại Ngu into the Ming empire."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà Minh là đế chế Trung Hoa từng có tác động và xâm lược vùng Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ming Dynasty; invaded Đại Ngu in 1407, leading to the collapse of the Hồ regime."</data>
