    <node id="&quot;PHÁP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""&lt;SEP&gt;"France invaded and colonized Vietnam, leading to incorporation into French Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"France is the colonial power referenced as the force behind colonial rule in Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Indochina, involved in postwar arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Indochina, whose troops were withdrawn from southern Vietnam under pressure from the United States and Ngô Đình Diệm's government."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power that invaded and controlled parts of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; provided support to Nguyễn Ánh during the campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; the European colonial power involved in early modern Vietnam's invasion and occupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; the colonial power involved via Bá Đa Lộc’s mission and the Versailles negotiations."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; the primary colonial ruler in Indochina and Vietnam, involved in multiple treaties and protectorates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đế quốc Pháp, lực lượng chiếm đóng Đông Dương."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, where the Versailles negotiations were mediated/hosted during Bá Đa Lộc’s mission to Nguyễn Ánh and allies."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; Allied power providing support to Nguyễn Ánh against Tây Sơn."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power in Indochina.""&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power in Indochina; participant in the Geneva Accords."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power occupying parts of Vietnam during and after WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonizer of Vietnam, integrating it into French Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"1940"&lt;&gt;"French colonial authorities; suppressed the uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;"1940"&lt;&gt;"French colonial authorities; suppressed the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Indochina that violently suppressed the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power referenced in relation to Vietnamese independence struggles."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power that attacked Haiphong in 1946 and later engaged in negotiations and the Indochina War."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power that expanded control over Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power that violently suppressed the Nam Kỳ uprising in Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; French forces that supported Nguyễn Ánh during his campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power that invaded Vietnam and annexed it into Indochina in 1887."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French government and military command in Indochina; involved in the Geneva Accords and the withdrawal from Indochina; France handed over control in 1954."&lt;SEP&gt;""&lt;|"The French colonial power in Indochina; fought against Vietnamese independence efforts and negotiated several treaties."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Indochina during 1940; cited as the oppressor in the Nam Kỳ context."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power in Indochina that violently suppressed the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"France, the colonial power opposing Vietnamese independence."_&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power in Indochina, participant in Geneva Accords."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power involved in the suppression."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power that ruled Vietnam, leading to incorporation into Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"French colonial power; invaded Vietnam and established protectorates and treaties."&lt;SEP&gt;"French government whose forces sought to reassert colonial control in Indochina after WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pháp là đế quốc thực dân đã tiến hành xâm chiếm Việt Nam và sáp nhập vào Liên bang Đông Dương năm 1887."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French forces allied with Nguyễn Ánh in the conflicts against Tây Sơn."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French government; referenced in treaties and negotiations with Vietnamese movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power in Indochina referenced as the oppressor against which Việt Minh and other Vietnamese factions resisted."&lt;SEP&gt;"France; colonial power whose treaties were canceled by the Provisional Government."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French colonial power in Vietnam, referenced as the colonizer whose domination was challenged by Việt Minh and the anti-colonial movement."_</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c2283fe59c1e2798b0a0aafedc3142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6033ac15f370150074084b2248ba04f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ca8856a3c05c7e29106b40dae03794b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0858721f576cf19954031c342a7d2bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3c75fb34fd08ca28a6bdea4defc0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
