    <node id="&quot;LIÊN BANG ĐÔNG DƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""&lt;SEP&gt;"1887"&lt;SEP&gt;"A French colonial-era federation in Indochina (Vietnam, Laos, and Cambodia) that was dissolved on 30 December 1954 as part of decolonization processes in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"A federation of protectorates and colonies in Indochina, officially formed in 1887 and constituting part of the Indochina Federation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation; formed in 1887, including An Nam, Bắc Kỳ and Nam Kỳ, later incorporating Cambodia and Laos."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Union under French rule; included Vietnam until the mid-20th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Union under French rule; included Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liên bang các nước Đông Dương bị giải thể hoàn toàn vào năm 1954."&lt;SEP&gt;"French Indochina Federation, formed through colonial consolidation in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"French Indochina Federation; established including Vietnam and parts of Southeast Asia.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation under French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation; colonial Indochina governance structure that was officially dissolved on 30 December 1954."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Federation of Indochina is a political entity that brought together protectorates and colonies in Vietnam; by 1887 these Vietnamese protectorates and colonies officially became constituent parts of the federation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A federation of French protectorates and colonies in Indochina, of which Vietnam was a component by 1887."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation; colonial political entity including Vietnam after 1887."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation; colonial political entity under French rule that included Vietnam as part of Indochina during the colonial era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation; officially dissolved in 1954 as decolonization progressed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liên bang Đông Dương (Indochina Federation), established in 1887, included An Nam (Trung Kỳ), Bắc Kỳ and Nam Kỳ, later incorporating Campuchia and Lào."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Federation of Indochina was a French colonial political entity in Southeast Asia that dissolved in 1954, marking the end of colonial governance in Indochina and paving the way for post-colonial arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Federation formed October 1887 including An Nam, Bắc Kỳ and Nam Kỳ; later Cambodia and Laos joined in 1893."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation under French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Federation; a colonial political entity dissolved on 30 December 1954, marking the end of French Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liên bang Đông Dương là liên minh thuộc Pháp, quản lý vùng Đông Dương thuộc Pháp."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Indochina Federation was a French-era political federation comprising protectorates and colonies in Vietnam, Laos, and Cambodia; it existed within the colonial framework during the late 19th and early 20th centuries (officially formed around 1887)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6033ac15f370150074084b2248ba04f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755</data>
      <data key="d3">1887&lt;SEP&gt;1954&lt;SEP&gt;1954"</data>
      <data key="d4">1887&lt;SEP&gt;AN NAM (TRUNG KỲ)&lt;SEP&gt;BẮC KỲ&lt;SEP&gt;CAMPUCHIA&lt;SEP&gt;INDOCHINA&lt;SEP&gt;INDOCHINA FEDERATION&lt;SEP&gt;INDOCHINA UNION&lt;SEP&gt;LIÊN BANG ĐÔNG DƯƠNG&lt;SEP&gt;LÀO&lt;SEP&gt;NAM KỲ&lt;SEP&gt;ĐÔNG DƯƠNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NHẬT BẢN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Country of origin of missionaries; listed alongside Bồ Đào Nha and Ý."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country whose traders and Jesuits interacted with Đại Việt; later a partner in diplomacy and trade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; imperial power that occupied parts of Vietnam during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; invaded Indochina during World War II and occupied the region.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; provided Western contact via traders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan, involved in trade and diplomacy with Đại Việt during the late 16th and early 17th centuries.&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; origin of missionaries mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan, whose merchants' ships traded in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; country of origin for some missionaries in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; formal diplomatic relations with Vietnam established in 1591; 34 letters exchanged with Mạc phủ Tokugawa between 1589 and 1612."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhật Bản (Japan), referenced as indirect support in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quân đội Nhật Bản đã xâm chiếm Đông Dương vào tháng 9 năm 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese Empire; occupied Indochina during WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where revolutionary groups operated and reformist ideas were fostered in this historical context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country where Phan Bội Châu and allies established the Duy Tân Hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội (in exile) and where much of the reformist activity took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Empire of Japan whose surrender allowed re-entry of French influence into Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan"&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; its forces invaded and occupied parts of Indochina in 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; referenced in the context of allied or opposing powers in the era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan; sent merchants and missionaries to Đại Việt; established relations in 1591."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan, the imperial power in World War II, opposed Việt Minh advances and controlled resources such as the Indochina Bank."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dab4a6d06213a3107d9e1ca29469f707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fca97c72fe1e0e81ac8addb98deb7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
