      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Empire of Japan, which occupied Vietnam for five years during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"Empire of Japan; occupied Vietnam during WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"Empire of Japan; occupied Vietnam during World War II; end of occupation noted in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Empire of Japan; destination for Vietnamese students via Đông Du and the country that exiled Phan Bội Châu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japanese Empire, invader in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese Empire, the destination for Vietnamese students sent by the Đông Du movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Empire that occupied Vietnam during World War II for about five years."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese Empire; host country where Phan Bội Châu and other Vietnamese reformists studied, a focal point for Đông Du movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese Empire that invaded Indochina in 1940; part of the occupation context in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese Empire; involved in exile of Vietnamese reformists."_&lt;SEP&gt;"Empire of Japan; occupying power in Vietnam during WWII; pressured to surrender."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese Empire occupying parts of Indochina during World War II, the principal foe of Việt Minh in the August Revolution."</data>
