    <node id="&quot;HOA KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""&lt;SEP&gt;""&lt;SEP&gt;"Chính thể VNCH nhận được sự can thiệp quân sự trực tiếp từ Hoa Kỳ; sự hiện diện quân sự của Mỹ tại miền Nam đạt đỉnh điểm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Kỳ công nhận Quốc gia Việt Nam vào ngày 3 tháng 2 năm 1950 và ký hiệp ước viện trợ kinh tế năm 1951."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States of America; key partner in Vietnam's diplomacy and defense modernization."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; Vietnam normalized diplomatic relations with the United States in 1995."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; ally of Việt Nam Cộng hòa during the Vietnam War."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; provided military and political backing to anti-communist South Vietnam and reorganized regional advisory structures (MAAG) in the Indochina theater."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Kỳ (United States), country with which Vietnam normalized diplomatic relations in 1995."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Kỳ (United States); country mentioned as skeptical about casualty statistics and referenced in the broader war context."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States; referenced as Obama's country and a key partner in Vietnam's normalization and military modernization."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States of America, ally and supporter of the Republic of Vietnam during the conflict."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; involved in diplomacy with Việt Nam, including embargo and normalization processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; key ally of VNCH, with direct military intervention and a peak troop presence in 1969 (543,000)."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; provided military aid to France and later supported anti-communist regimes in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States government; mentioned in the text in the context of casualty statistics related to Vietnam War."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States opposed Vietnam's normalization efforts and maintained harsh sanctions since 1975."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States, which normalized relations with Vietnam after the 2016 visit; the U.S. lifted the arms embargo, enabling Vietnam to purchase modern defense equipment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States; it provided military aid to France from 1950 onward and later supported anti-communist regimes in Vietnam; it reorganized MAAG."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States; its military presence in the South peaked in April 1969 at about 543,000 troops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States; officially recognizes the State of Vietnam in 1950 and establishes diplomatic relations, and later signs a treaty for aid in 1951."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; Vietnam normalized relations with the U.S. in 1995."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; supported Việt Nam Cộng hòa and opposed the DRV in the Vietnam War."&lt;SEP&gt;"1950"&lt;|"The United States; formally recognized the State of Vietnam in 1950 and provided economic and later military aid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Kỳ (United States) is mentioned in the context of Vietnam–U.S. relations and the lifting of an arms embargo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Kỳ là nước đồng minh và hậu thuẫn Việt Nam Cộng hòa trong cuộc chiến tranh Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States, a major external power involved in the conflict; military presence in the South peaked around 543,000 troops in 1969."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States; imposed an embargo on Vietnam since 1975 and pursued normalization later, including Clinton's 2000 visit."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; diplomatic relations with Vietnam normalized in 1995."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; provided military aid from 1950 onward and later backed anti-communist South Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States; mentioned as part of the Western Allies context alongside Tây Âu and Liên Xô."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e1e11930ab01fb061749acffe85b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4549a0a33a97f39084dfcd2d857e18f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df404f664a0d60546a9e31eb5bdff3ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ffd57cec3dd07166a619a76148c755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4820a393047d71ddfc9dd25445f040a</data>
      <data key="d3">1945&lt;SEP&gt;1950&lt;SEP&gt;1950"&lt;SEP&gt;1969&lt;SEP&gt;1994&lt;SEP&gt;2016</data>
      <data key="d4">HOA KỲ&lt;SEP&gt;HOA KỲ (THE UNITED STATES) MAINTAINED AN EMBARGO ON VIETNAM AND BEGAN NORMALIZATION PROCESSES&lt;SEP&gt;UNITED STATES&lt;SEP&gt;UNITED STATES; USA&lt;SEP&gt;US&lt;SEP&gt;USA&lt;SEP&gt;WITH THE EMBARGO LIFTING ANNOUNCED IN 1994 AND FORMAL NORMALIZATION BY 1995; CLINTON VISITED VIETNAM IN 2000.</data>
