    <node id="&quot;VIỆT NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Southeast Asian country central to the historical narrative, including wars, diplomacy, and reform efforts described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country that established diplomatic relations with Japan in 1591."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country/region in Southeast Asia where the earliest rice-farming communities and floodplain societies appeared; includes sites such as Mán Bạc and Núi Nấp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation discussed in nationalist context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation in Southeast Asia; central to the works cited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation that became part of the Silk Road by sea."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country at the center of this historical narrative; broader political and diplomatic context with foreign powers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam, a Southeast Asian country undergoing economic transformation; faces territorial disputes with Cambodia and China, and is categorized among the Next Eleven economies; engages in diplomacy with the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is the country involved in border disputes with China, engaged in a Cambodian conflict (1979–1989) with a reform program (Đổi Mới) initiated in 1986, and later moving toward rapprochement with the United States and integration into the global economy (WTO in 2007)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation involved in the Indochina colonial period.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation name formalized under the Nguyễn dynasty; previously variants include Đại Việt, An Nam, Nam Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country involved in the war and postwar era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam is the country/region involved in the colonial and nationalist history described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam transformed from one of the world's poorest countries into a middle-income economy within a generation, marking a major economic transition beginning in 1986."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam; country discussed in the sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is a Southeast Asian country central to regional conflicts and diplomacy in this text: invaded by China in 1979, later faced diplomatic isolation in the 1980s, initiated Đổi Mới reforms in 1986; conducted military operations in Cambodia (1979–1989); pursuing economic reforms and global integration culminating in WTO membership in 2007."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam, a Southeast Asian country described in this text, whose modern history in the passage includes leadership in 1976, border wars with China (1979) and Cambodia (1978–1989), economic reforms (Đổi Mới) beginning by 1986, and subsequent diplomatic normalization with China (1991) and the United States (1995), along with notes on modern demographics and archaeological findings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Southeast Asian nation that experienced major wars, economic reform, and shifts in international relations during the late 20th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in Southeast Asia referenced within the Indochina colonial context."&lt;SEP&gt;"A unified socialist republic formed in 1976 following the end of the division."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country in Southeast Asia; context includes northern tombs Mán Bạc and Núi Nấp, and later Khmer polities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical Vietnam discussed in context of internal reform, Catholic persecution, and external relations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam is a Southeast Asian country that began a major transformation in 1986, shifting from one of the world's poorest nations to a middle-income economy within a generation; it faces territorial disputes with neighbors, notably Cambodia along the land border and China in the South China Sea; it has pursued closer relations with the United States, becoming an emerging industrial economy and a regional middle power, and is associated with the Next Eleven group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is a Southeast Asian country involved in border disputes with China, allied with the Soviet Union, engaged in Cambodia (1979–1989), undertook Đổi Mới reforms, and progressed toward WTO membership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is the country central to the described events, including Tây Sơn-era conflicts and Nguyễn Ánh's campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is the country involved in organizing the first general election in 1946. It becomes the emerging independent polity during the postwar period, leading to constitutional developments and the struggle against colonial authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam"&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam, the country referenced in the historical narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đất nước cổ đại và hiện đại, nơi các nền văn hóa đầu khai phát triển và là phần của tuyến Con đường ngọc bích trên biển."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Southeast Asian country referenced throughout the text; site of the Nguyễn dynasty and the French colonial incursions described."&lt;SEP&gt;"A country that became part of the Silk Road by sea."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"A socialist republic in Southeast Asia; involved in border conflicts with China (1979) and Cambodia (1978–1989); experienced a severe economic crisis and implemented Đổi Mới reforms from 1986; later normalized diplomatic relations with China (1991) and the United States (1995); home to 54 ethnic groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country in Southeast Asia; site of ancient tomb sites Mán Bạc and Núi Nấp and key to prehistoric migrations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country referenced in the context of its revolutionary struggle and independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation discussed in the historical context; historically referred to as An Nam before the adoption of Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation/region at the center of the Vietnam War historiography."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc gia; tham gia Comecon; ký hiệp ước với Liên Xô; thống nhất đất nước."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam, the country referenced as the focus of nationalist movements within Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is a Southeast Asian country at the center of regional and global diplomatic and economic developments described in the text: it faced Chinese military pressure in 1979, engaged in complex relations with the United States, the Soviet Union, and China; implemented Đổi Mới reforms from 1986, played a leading role in Cambodia's geopolitics, and later integrated into the world economy by joining the WTO in 2007."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is described as having transformed from one of the world's poorest countries into a middle-income economy within one generation, while facing territorial disputes with neighbors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đất nước thống nhất sau 1975; thành lập nhà nước xã hội chủ nghĩa vào năm 1976."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country emerging from colonial rule during the postwar upheaval described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nation of Southeast Asia central to the events described (the August 1945 revolution and subsequent independence)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam is the country referenced as achieving independence in 1945 according to the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e1e11930ab01fb061749acffe85b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01995274690fe1835d7836e3a481a678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc55d62fe8c98a4db1992322d16a5280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c2283fe59c1e2798b0a0aafedc3142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f2f053f1c7eb75498d3b31a687c2e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df404f664a0d60546a9e31eb5bdff3ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dab4a6d06213a3107d9e1ca29469f707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4820a393047d71ddfc9dd25445f040a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
      <data key="d3">1591&lt;SEP&gt;1802&lt;SEP&gt;1945&lt;SEP&gt;1946&lt;SEP&gt;1976&lt;SEP&gt;1979&lt;SEP&gt;1986</data>
