    <node id="&quot;ĐẾ QUỐC LA MÃ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mối liên hệ thương mại phương Tây với xứ An Nam bắt nguồn từ đoàn thương buôn của Đế quốc La Mã và sau đó được Marco Polo mở rộng."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phái đoàn sứ bộ từ Đế quốc La Mã đến Trung Hoa đi qua tuyến đường này; các đoàn thương buôn cũng theo sau."."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roman Empire, referenced as early Western contact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roman Empire; earliest Western traders are mentioned as part of the Western contact with An Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roman Empire; mentioned as sending the first delegation to China in 166."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire is cited as sending the first diplomatic mission that passed along the described route, indicating early long-distance contact and trade with East Asia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roman Empire; its first delegation reached China in the year 166, signaling early East–West contact."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire referenced as part of early Western contact with An Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire; the first envoy from Rome to China is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roman Empire; mentioned as the origin of a scribe's journey to China."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire is referenced as the origin of Western merchants who interacted with xứ An Nam, preceding Marco Polo's visit.""&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire, referenced as the source of the earliest Roman delegation to China in 166."&lt;SEP&gt;"Western empire whose merchants arrived in the region; early contact channel."</data>
