    <node id="&quot;AN NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""&lt;SEP&gt;"0866"&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam (central Vietnam); part of the Indochina Federation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam is described as a thriving port-centered region that became a Tang protectorate, serving as a hub for goods moving via inland and coastal routes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam is the historical region studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for the territory later called Việt Nam; used in the context of historical naming in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam (Trung Kỳ) region within Indochina.""&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam was renamed to Tĩnh Hải quân in 866."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Vietnam used in the context of early Western contact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical region in what is now northern Vietnam under Tang Dynasty administration; later serves as a key port/market area and capital in various periods, including governance under An Nam đô hộ phủ."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam is the historic name used by Chinese dynasties for Đại Việt; referenced in naming debates."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam is the historical reference for the Vietnamese realm discussed in Western contact.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical region renamed to Tĩnh Hải quân in 866."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam is the historical name of the Vietnamese region which, in 866, was renamed to Tĩnh Hải quân."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central/Northern Vietnam region; part of French Indochina as An Nam (Trung Kỳ)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name used for Vietnam before adopting Việt Nam."</data>
