      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1010"&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynasty of Vietnam (Lý) that centralized power and maintained nominal tributary relations with the Song."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lý dynasty; Vietnamese imperial dynasty established by Lý Công Uẩn (1010–1400)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triều Lý (the Lý dynasty) was the Vietnamese ruling dynasty founded by Lý Công Uẩn, which established governance, national consolidation, and cultural institutions during its rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lý dynasty that ruled Vietnam; established by Lý Công Uẩn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese dynasty (10th–13th centuries) that centralized power and engaged with the Song dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ly dynasty; centralized royal power and maintained tribute to the Song (Nhà Tống) while remaining autonomous."</data>
