    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOẠN 12 SỨ QUÂN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">""Loạn 12 sứ quân denotes a period of fragmentation by local warlords challenging central authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loạn 12 sứ quân was the first large-scale civil war among local feudal lords in Vietnam, leading to consolidation under Đinh Bộ Lĩnh."&lt;SEP&gt;"A 10th-century rebellion of 12 warlords against central authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"The first major civil war in the country, triggered by internal rivalries and the subsequent campaigns that culminate in Đinh Bộ Lĩnh's unification by 968."&lt;SEP&gt;"Period of fragmentation by 12 local warlords; historical power gaps among rival leaders."&lt;SEP&gt;"The first large-scale civil war in Vietnam, triggered by the power struggle after Ngô Xương Văn's death in 965."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loạn 12 sứ quân was a large-scale war among twelve local lords that Đinh Bộ Lĩnh eventually pacified and overcame in 968."&lt;SEP&gt;"The '12 Warlords' rebellion, a period of fragmentation in which twelve local Vietnamese rulers vied for power before central unification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6033ac15f370150074084b2248ba04f3</data>
      <data key="d3">965</data>
      <data key="d4">""'&lt;SEP&gt;12 SỨ QUÂN&lt;SEP&gt;LOẠN 12 SỨ QUÂN</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HẬU LƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">""Hậu Lương is the Chinese dynasty to which the Tĩnh Hải quân paid tribute for political recognition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chinese dynasty to which Tĩnh Hải quân paid tribute in exchange for political recognition."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Later Liang (Hou Liang) dynasty of China; a political authority that the Tĩnh Hải quân paid tribute to in order to gain political recognition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6033ac15f370150074084b2248ba04f3</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">HOU LIANG&lt;SEP&gt;HẬU LƯƠNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DƯƠNG TAM KHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese noble who usurped the throne from Ngô Quyền's eldest son, Ngô Xương Ngập."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brother-in-law of Ngô Quyền who seized the throne after Quyền's death."|"&lt;SEP&gt;"Dương Tam Kha is a historical figure who seized the throne formerly held by Ngô Xương Ngập, initiating a dynastic power struggle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brother-in-law who usurped the throne from Ngô Xương Ngập."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dương Tam Kha is a historical figure who seized the throne from Ngô Quyền's eldest son Ngô Xương Ngập."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dương Tam Kha is a powerful figure who usurped the throne from Ngô Xương Ngập, Ngô Quyền's eldest son."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dương Tam Kha, Ngô Quyền's brother-in-law, seized the throne from Ngô Xương Ngập."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6033ac15f370150074084b2248ba04f3</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">""'&lt;SEP&gt;DƯƠNG TAM KHA</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐINH BỘ LĨNH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Military leader who defeats the twelve warlords, establishes the Đinh dynasty, and renames the country from Tĩnh Hải quân to Đại Cồ Việt; makes Hoa Lư his capital."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đinh Bộ Lĩnh is the warlord who defeated the 12 local lords, unified the country, founded the Đinh dynasty, and renamed the state to Đại Cồ Việt; capital Hoa Lư."&lt;SEP&gt;"Military leader who pacified the 12 warlords by 968, founded the Đinh dynasty, and moved the capital to Hoa Lư; renamed the country Đại Cồ Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đinh Bộ Lĩnh united the twelve sứ quân to reunify the country, founded the Đinh dynasty in 968, and renamed the state from Tĩnh Hải quân to Đại Cồ Việt; he made Hoa Lư the capital."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d</data>
      <data key="d3">968</data>
      <data key="d4">""'&lt;SEP&gt;ANGLIFIED: ĐINH TIÊN HOÀNG&lt;SEP&gt;ĐINH BỘ LĨNH&lt;SEP&gt;ĐINH TIÊN HOÀNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẠI CỒ VIỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historic name of the Vietnamese state before the capital relocation; its capital was Hoa Lư before moving to Đại La."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Vietnam after renaming from Tĩnh Hải quân; capital at Hoa Lư."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical predecessor state of Đại Việt; its capital was Hoa Lư."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đại Cồ Việt is the state established by Đinh Bộ Lĩnh after renaming Tĩnh Hải quân; capital was Hoa Lư."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese kingdom renamed from Tĩnh Hải quân; capital at Hoa Lư."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đại Cồ Việt was the name of the Vietnamese state whose capital was moved by Lý Công Uẩn from Hoa Lư to Đại La."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese state formed by Đinh Bộ Lĩnh; renamed from Tĩnh Hải quân."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese state founded by Đinh Bộ Lĩnh in 968 after unifying the twelve sứ quân; renamed from Tĩnh Hải quân, with Hoa Lư as the capital."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c</data>
      <data key="d3">968</data>
      <data key="d4">""'&lt;SEP&gt;TĨNH HẢI QUÂN&lt;SEP&gt;ĐẠI CỒ VIỆT</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOA LƯ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient capital of Đại Cồ Việt, described as being fortified by mountains and rivers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Lư was the capital of Đại Cồ Việt, located in present-day Ninh Bình."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital of Đại Cồ Việt established by Đinh Bộ Lĩnh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital of Đại Cồ Việt established by Đinh Bộ Lĩnh; located in present-day Ninh Bình."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Lư was the political capital of Đại Cồ Việt before the capital moved to Đại La under Lý Công Uẩn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital city of Đại Cồ Việt, located at Hoa Lư in Ninh Bình."&lt;SEP&gt;"Old capital of Đại Cồ Việt before the capital relocation by Lý Công Uẩn in 1010."&lt;SEP&gt;"The old capital of Đại Cồ Việt; the capital moved from Hoa Lư to Đại La."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoa Lư (Ninh Bình) was the capital of Đại Cồ Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"The original capital of Đại Cồ Việt, later replaced when the capital moved to Đại La."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c</data>
