    <node id="&quot;LÝ CÔNG UẨN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A high-ranking military commander who was later revered as emperor and founder of the Lý dynasty; in 1010 he moved the capital through Chiếu dời đô."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lý Công Uẩn, later founder of the Lý dynasty after being proclaimed emperor."&lt;SEP&gt;"A high-ranking official who, after Lê Long Đĩnh's death in 1009, was enthroned and founded the Ly dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Founder of the Lý dynasty; unified power and initiated a new imperial era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lý Công Uẩn was a high-ranking military leader who, after the death of Lê Long Đĩnh in 1009, was unanimously proclaimed emperor and founded the Lý dynasty; he also moved and renamed the capital."&lt;SEP&gt;"Founder of the Lý dynasty; ascended to the throne and initiated the Lý era in 1009."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lý Công Uẩn was a senior military leader who was proclaimed emperor, founding the Ly dynasty; in 1010 he moved the capital from Hoa Lư to Đại La and later renamed Đại La to Thăng Long."&lt;SEP&gt;"A high-ranking military leader in the capital who, after the chaotic years following Lê Hoàn's death, was unanimously proclaimed emperor; he founded the Lý dynasty, moved the capital from Đại Cồ Việt's Hoa Lư to Đại La in 1010, and later oversaw the renaming of Đại La to Thăng Long."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lý Công Uẩn was the official who, aided by the court, was proclaimed emperor and founded the Lý dynasty."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27e11721fea6555c621a81136e468f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c</data>
      <data key="d3">1009&lt;SEP&gt;1010</data>
      <data key="d4">""'&lt;SEP&gt;LÝ CÔNG UẨN</data>
    </node>
