      <data key="d4">GIAO THƯ NHẬT BẢN-VIỆT NAM</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THỜI KỲ TRỊNH–NGUYỄN PHÂN TRANH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Khu vực Trịnh–Nguyễn phân tranh kéo dài từ 1600 đến 1777 trong văn bản."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dab4a6d06213a3107d9e1ca29469f707</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">THỜI KỲ TRỊNH–NGUYỄN PHÂN TRANH</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN HOÀNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nguyễn Hoàng is the founder of the Nguyễn lords in the south (Đàng Trong). In 1600 he formally proclaimed himself Chúa (the title 'Vương' as used in popular speech) and ended paying taxes or providing military support to the Trịnh; he also moved the capital to Phú Xuân (present-day Huế)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Hoàng was a Vietnamese provincial ruler who, in 1600, formally declared the title of Chúa (often referred to as Vương) and ended paying tribute or providing troops to the Trịnh; he also moved the capital to Phú Xuân (present-day Huế), establishing a southern administration and resisting Trịnh subordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Hoàng, a prominent Nguyễn lord who established control in the south, declared Chúa in 1600, and moved the capital to Phú Xuân."&lt;SEP&gt;"The fourth son of Nguyễn Kim who moved south to govern Thuận Hóa–Quảng Nam in 1558, establishing southern Đàng Trong.""&lt;SEP&gt;"The fourth son of Nguyễn Kim who moved south to govern Thuận Hóa–Quảng Nam in 1558.&lt;SEP&gt;"Son of Nguyễn Kim; moved to the south in 1558, consolidating Đàng Trong (Thuận Hóa–Quảng Nam) and building southern power."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Hoàng officially proclaimed the title Chúa (Vương) and moved the capital to Phú Xuân (present-day Huế), ending tax collection and military support to the Trịnh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Son of Nguyễn Kim; moved south to govern Thuận Hóa–Quảng Nam and laid the groundwork for Đàng Trong."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dab4a6d06213a3107d9e1ca29469f707</data>
      <data key="d3">1558&lt;SEP&gt;1600&lt;SEP&gt;1600"</data>
      <data key="d4">CHÚA&lt;SEP&gt;CHÚA NGUYỄN&lt;SEP&gt;CHÚA TIÊN NGUYỄN HOÀNG&lt;SEP&gt;NGUYỄN HOÀNG&lt;SEP&gt;VƯƠNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN PHÚC NGUYÊN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Con trai thứ sáu của Nguyễn Hoàng lên nối nghiệp và tiếp tục chính sách độc lập với họ Trịnh, duy trì lễ phụng vua Lê."&lt;SEP&gt;"Con trai thứ sáu của Nguyễn Hoàng; he ascended to power in 1613 and continued the Nguyễn policy of independence from the Trịnh while nominally honoring the Lê imperial line."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Phúc Nguyên, son of Nguyễn Hoàng, succeeded him in 1613 and continued policies to resist Trịnh influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Phúc Nguyên is the sixth son of Nguyễn Hoàng who succeeded him in 1613, continuing a policy of resisting submission to the Trịnh while keeping nominal allegiance to the Lê throne.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2</data>
      <data key="d3">1613&lt;SEP&gt;1613"</data>
      <data key="d4">NGUYỄN PHÚC NGUYÊN</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRỊNH TRÁNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trịnh Tráng ascended the throne in 1623 after the death of his father Trịnh Tùng; he led major campaigns against Nguyễn Phúc Nguyên, although his campaign in the south was ultimately unsuccessful.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Trịnh Tráng ascended the throne in 1623 after the death of his father Trịnh Tùng; he led major campaigns and pursued expansion, including an offensive in 1627."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trịnh Tráng became chúa in 1623 after Trịnh Tùng's death and led major campaigns into the south, including a 1627 invasion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trịnh Tráng lên nối ngôi sau khi cha là Trịnh Tùng qua đời; lãnh đạo quân Trịnh và tham gia chiến dịch lớn vào Nam against Nguyễn Phúc Nguyên."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2</data>
      <data key="d3">1623&lt;SEP&gt;1623"</data>
      <data key="d4">TRỊNH&lt;SEP&gt;TRỊNH TRÁNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN PHÚC TẦN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chúa Nguyễn sau khi nghị hòa với Trịnh, tiếp tục quyền lực ở Đàng Trong và đối đầu thông qua các đàm phán cuối cùng 1672."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chúa Nguyễn who engaged in negotiations and concluded a truce (nghị hòa) with Trịnh Tạc in 1672."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Phúc Tần was the Nguyễn lord who negotiated peace with Trịnh Tạc in 1672."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Phúc Tần was a Nguyễn lord who, after the Trịnh Tráng campaigns, engaged in ceasefire and reconciliation with Trịnh Tạc in 1672.""</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2</data>
      <data key="d3">1672&lt;SEP&gt;1672"</data>
      <data key="d4">NGUYỄN PHÚC TẦN</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALEXANDRE DE RHODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alexandre de Rhodes was a Jesuit missionary whose work helped Latinize Vietnamese writing; published an early Western map of An Nam in 1651."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jesuit priest, a major influence in Vietnam; completed the Latin-based Vietnamese script (Chữ Quốc ngữ) and contributed to a Vietnamese–Portuguese–Latin dictionary published in 1651."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alexandre de Rhodes, a Jesuit missionary, had a major influence in Vietnam; he published the Latin–Vietnamese dictionary Từ điển Việt–Bồ–La (Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum) in 1651 and contributed to Western contact with xứ An Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jesuit missionary who helped lay the groundwork for Catholicism in Vietnam and Latinized Vietnamese script; alias Đắc Lộ."&lt;SEP&gt;"Một nhà truyền giáo Dòng Tên có ảnh hưởng lớn tại Việt Nam; hoàn thiện hệ chữ Latinh hóa và biên soạn từ điển Việt–Bồ–La được xuất bản năm 1651."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2</data>
      <data key="d3">1651&lt;SEP&gt;1651"</data>
      <data key="d4">ALEXANDRE DE RHODES&lt;SEP&gt;ĐẮC LỘ</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIROLAMO MAIORICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
