      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dòng Tên (Society of Jesus) is a Catholic religious order that played a central role in missionary activities in Vietnam and worked alongside other orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dòng Tên (Society of Jesus) played a major role in the introduction and spread of Christianity in Đàng Ngoài and Đàng Trong; Alexandre de Rhodes is described as a priest in this order.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Dòng Tên is the Vietnamese name for the Society of Jesus, a Catholic religious order involved in early missionary work in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jesuit order whose priests in the 17th century laid the foundations for Catholicism in both Đàng Trong and Đàng Ngoài in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jesuit order, central to missionary activity in Vietnam as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Jesuit order mentioned as a major source of missionary activity in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Jesuit order, influential in 17th-century Vietnam as missionaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jesuit order, central to Catholic missionary activity in 17th-century Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tổ chức truyền giáo Công giáo, có vai trò then chốt trong sự kiện Công giáo tại Việt Nam và là quê hương của Alexandre de Rhodes."</data>
