    <node id="&quot;NGHĨA QUÂN TÂY SƠN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nghia quan Tay Son was a rising military movement that rapidly attracted a broad cross-section of society in the Tây Nguyên region, including poor peasants, artisans, Christian parishioners, ethnic minorities, and later Chinese merchants; it sought to abolish the heavy taxes imposed by the Nguyễn lords and expanded its influence across Đại Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nghĩa quân Tây Sơn is a peasant- and artisan-based rebel force in the Tây Sơn region that emerged to challenge the Nguyễn lords, and by 1776 had conquered the Đàng Trong territory of the Nguyễn lords."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nghĩa quân Tây Sơn is a peasant-based revolutionary army that mobilized poor villagers, artisans, Catholic laypeople, minority groups, and Hoa merchants; it challenged the Nguyễn lords and expanded control over Đàng Trong, reaching prominence by 1776."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tây Sơn rebel army, which rapidly gathered support from peasants, artisans, Catholics, ethnic minorities, and Hoa merchants; by 1776 it had seized Đàng Trong from the Nguyễn lords."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ca8856a3c05c7e29106b40dae03794b</data>
      <data key="d3">1776</data>
