    <node id="&quot;BÁ ĐA LỘC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A French ecclesiastical envoy who sought French military support for Nguyễn Ánh and served as intermediary in negotiations for the Versailles Treaty; he later returned to Vietnam with ships and volunteers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A French envoy serving Nguyễn Ánh who organized volunteers and supported reform of the Nguyễn Ánh navy; died in 1799."&lt;SEP&gt;"A French official who led a group of French volunteers that returned to Vietnam in 1788; he organized Nguyễn Ánh's naval forces in European style and contributed to the defeat of the Tây Sơn navy at Quy Nhơn in 1792; he died in 1799."&lt;SEP&gt;"French diplomat who mediated between Nguyễn Ánh and France; organized negotiations for the Versailles treaty in 1787. Also known as Pigneaux de Behaine."&lt;SEP&gt;"French advisor; led volunteers who assisted Nguyễn Ánh, including Jean-Marie Dayot; played a key role in organizing Nguyễn Ánh's naval forces."&lt;SEP&gt;"French diplomat and intermediary who negotiated the Versailles Treaty (1787) and later pursued support for Nguyễn Ánh; associated with Puducherry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bá Đa Lộc is the commander whose volunteers included Jean-Marie Dayot; he oversaw efforts aiding Nguyễn Ánh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bá Đa Lộc, a French bishop (Pigneaux de Behaine), acted as a mediator and brokered French support for Nguyễn Ánh; he returned to Vietnam afterward."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ca8856a3c05c7e29106b40dae03794b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461</data>
