    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN ÁNH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Nguyễn dynasty prince (Nguyễn Phúc Ánh) who fled to Siam for aid, later returned with Siamese forces to attempt to regain power; associated with Gia Định."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heir of the Nguyễn Lords; fled to Siam (Xiêm La) to seek military aid, returned with Siamese forces, and recaptured Gia Định in 1788; built a base there."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leader of the Nguyễn faction who later became Emperor Gia Long; he consolidated control of Saigon, captured Phú Xuân (Huế) by 1801 and ultimately defeated Tây Sơn forces to unify the country by 1802; he received support from France, Chinese communities, Siam, and Catholic converts during his campaigns, establishing the Nguyễn dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese ruler who unified south, defeated Tây Sơn, captured Phú Xuân, and founded the Nguyễn dynasty as Gia Long."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese ruler who allied with French forces, Hoa kiều, Siamese, and Christian followers; founded the Nguyễn dynasty as Gia Long."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese ruler who ultimately founded the Nguyễn dynasty (as Gia Long), allied with French, Chinese, Siamese, and Catholics; captured Huế in 1801 and ascended the throne in 1802."&lt;SEP&gt;"A claimant of the Nguyễn lineage who fled to Siam after losing power to the Tây Sơn; returned with a Siamese force to recapture Gia Định and fought to reclaim power from Tây Sơn."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ca8856a3c05c7e29106b40dae03794b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461</data>
