    <node id="&quot;PHAN BỘI CHÂU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese nationalist and reformist who initiated the Đông Du movement in 1905 and helped found the revolutionary groups Duy Tân Hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội in Japan; commonly known by the alias Sào Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"A key Vietnamese revolutionary thinker who founded the Đông Du movement; co-founded Duy Tân Hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội in Japan; alias Sào Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"A leading Vietnamese nationalist reformer who spearheaded the Đông Du movement and helped found Duy Tân Hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội; also known by the alias Sào Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu is a Vietnamese nationalist revolutionary who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou to organize resistance against French colonial rule; he was kidnapped by French secret police in Shanghai in 1925 and later placed under house arrest at Bến Ngự (Huế) until his death in 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese patriot who initiated the Đông Du movement in 1905 and, with Kỳ Ngoại hầu Cường Để, founded Duy Tân hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội in Japan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu was a Vietnamese nationalist who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Canton (Quảng Châu) to advocate modernization and armed struggle against French rule; in 1925 French secret police kidnapped him in Shanghai (Thượng Hải); he was later kept under house arrest at Bến Ngự (Huế) until his death in 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu là nhà cách mạng Việt Nam, thành lập Việt Nam Quang phục Hội tại Quảng Châu và lên kế hoạch đấu tranh vũ trang; bị mật thám Pháp bắt cóc tại Thượng Hải năm 1925; sau đó bị giam lỏng tại Huế cho đến khi qua đời."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu is a Vietnamese nationalist revolutionary who founded Vietnamese nationalist organizations and led early anti-French activities; he was kidnapped in Shanghai in 1925, later imprisoned in Huế, and died in 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese nationalist thinker and reformer; referenced in the text as a possible 'saint' in the sấm truyền, though he died in 1940."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
      <data key="d3">1905&lt;SEP&gt;1925&lt;SEP&gt;1940</data>
      <data key="d4">PHAN BOI CHAU&lt;SEP&gt;PHAN BỘI CHÂU&lt;SEP&gt;SÀO NAM</data>
    </node>
