    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUỐC TẾ CỘNG SẢN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comintern, the international communist organization that directed Vietnamese movements; it dispatched Nguyễn Ái Quốc to Hong Kong to lead unity talks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc tế Cộng sản (Comintern) coordinated unification of Indochinese communist groups and supported the formation of the Vietnamese Communist Party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tổ chức Cộng sản quốc tế (Comintern) đã cử Nguyễn Ái Quốc tới Hồng Kông để chủ trì hội nghị hợp nhất các tổ chức cộng sản Việt Nam thành Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">COMINTERN&lt;SEP&gt;QUỐC TẾ CỘNG SẢN</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN ÁI QUỐC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alias of Ho Chi Minh; described as a potential leader of Việt Minh and tied to Nam Đàn (Nghệ An)."(&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Ái Quốc is a Vietnamese revolutionary who operated in France from 1911, helped found the French Communist Party, and in 1924 went to the Soviet Union to work for the Communist International (Comintern); in the late 1920s he acted as a representative of the Comintern to build and lead communist movements in Southeast Asia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudonym of Hồ Chí Minh; participated in founding the French Communist Party, and by the late 1920s worked with the Comintern to guide Communist movements in Southeast Asia; went to the Soviet Union in 1924 to work for the Comintern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Ái Quốc là một nhà cách mạng Việt Nam, còn được biết đến với bí danh Hồ Chí Minh; tham gia sáng lập Đảng Cộng sản Pháp, được cử tham gia hợp nhất các tổ chức cộng sản ở Đông Dương, lãnh đạo Việt Minh và hoạt động trong và với Quốc tế Cộng sản."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
      <data key="d3">1941&lt;SEP&gt;1945</data>
      <data key="d4">HỒ CHÍ MINH&lt;SEP&gt;NGUYỄN ÁI QUỐC</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MẶT TRẬN VIỆT MINH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Established in 1941 as a broad front led by the Communist movement to fight for independence; de facto led by the Communist Party; later coordinated with the OSS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist front led by Hồ Chí Minh that orchestrated independence efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mặt trận Việt Minh was formed in 1941 as a broad anti-colonial alliance led in practice by the Communist Party of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Viet Minh political‑military front; also referred to as Việt Minh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liên minh rộng rãi tập hợp mọi tầng lớp đấu tranh vì độc lập và một nhà nước dân chủ, do Đảng Cộng sản lãnh đạo."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese nationalist front represented by Hồ Chí Minh; played a central role in the independence movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Việt Minh, a broad resistance front formed in 1941 under Hồ Chí Minh to coordinate anti-imperial efforts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
      <data key="d3">1941&lt;SEP&gt;1945&lt;SEP&gt;1945"</data>
      <data key="d4">MẶT TRẬN VIỆT MINH&lt;SEP&gt;VIET MINH&lt;SEP&gt;VIET-MINH&lt;SEP&gt;VIỆT MINH</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Office of Strategic Services (US wartime intelligence agency) that cooperated with the Việt Minh to defeat Japanese forces in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Office of Strategic Services, wartime US intelligence agency; the Việt Minh coordinated with OSS during WWII to share intelligence on Japanese activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States Office of Strategic Services; cooperated with Việt Minh to share intelligence about the Japanese."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Office of Strategic Services (OSS), a US WWII intelligence agency, partnered with Việt Minh to defeat Japanese forces in Thái Nguyên."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
      <data key="d3">1945</data>
      <data key="d4">OFFICE OF STRATEGIC SERVICES&lt;SEP&gt;OSS</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HỒNG KÔNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hong Kong, the site of Nguyễn Ái Quốc's 1930 conference to unify Vietnamese communist groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong, where Nguyễn Ái Quốc was sent by the Comintern to oversee unity talks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hồng Kông was a base for Nguyễn Ái Quốc's efforts to unite the communist groups into Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Năm 1930, Quốc tế Cộng sản cử Nguyễn Ái Quốc tới Hồng Kông để chủ trì hội nghị hợp nhất các tổ chức cộng sản Việt Nam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
      <data key="d3">1930</data>
      <data key="d4">HONG KONG&lt;SEP&gt;HỒNG KÔNG</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẾ QUỐC VIỆT NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A brief, nominal empire proclaimed by Bao Dai in 1945 in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chính thể ngắn ngủi được tuyên bố thành lập bởi Hoàng đế Bảo Đại trong thời gian Nhật chiếm đóng."&lt;SEP&gt;"The short-lived Vietnamese empire proclaimed by Hoàng đế Bảo Đại."&lt;SEP&gt;"The short-lived state proclaimed by Emperor Bao Dai during Japanese occupation in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"The short‑lived imperial state proclaimed by Emperor Bao Dai in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đế quốc Việt Nam was the short-lived empire proclaimed by Hoàng đế Bảo Đại during the period of Japanese control."&lt;SEP&gt;"A short-lived imperial regime proclaimed by Emperor Bảo Đại under Japanese protection following the 1945 coup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short-lived Japanese-supported state proclaimed in Vietnam during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"Empire of Vietnam; the regime under which Trần Trọng Kim served as prime minister."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical Vietnamese empire/government under Japanese influence mentioned in the context of the wartime period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Empire of Vietnam, the regime under Bao Đại that held central authority during Japanese occupation and was compelled to transfer power in August 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese Empire; referenced as the colonial regime that did not convene a public reading of the declaration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The puppet imperial regime supported by Japan in Vietnam, resisting transfer of power to Việt Minh."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18d8e97a0e4680cead04b467abbaf21b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
      <data key="d3">1945&lt;SEP&gt;1945"</data>
      <data key="d4">"")&lt;SEP&gt;EMPIRE OF VIETNAM&lt;SEP&gt;ĐẾ QUỐC VIỆT NAM</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOÀNG ĐẾ BẢO ĐẠI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emperor who proclaimed the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who proclaimed the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam under Japanese protection and appointed Trần Trọng Kim as Prime Minister."&lt;SEP&gt;"The emperor who briefly proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam and abdicated in August 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoàng đế Bảo Đại was the emperor under Japanese occupation who declared the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoàng đế tuyên bố thành lập Đế quốc Việt Nam dưới sự bảo hộ của Nhật Bản."&lt;SEP&gt;"The emperor who declared the short-lived Empire of Vietnam and appointed Trần Trọng Kim as Prime Minister."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who, under Japanese protection, proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam and appointed Trần Trọng Kim as Prime Minister; abdicated later in 1945."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
      <data key="d3">1945&lt;SEP&gt;1945"</data>
      <data key="d4">"")&lt;SEP&gt;BAO DAI&lt;SEP&gt;BẢO ĐẠI&lt;SEP&gt;HOÀNG ĐẾ BẢO ĐẠI</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRẦN PHÚ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First General Secretary of the Vietnamese Communist Party after unification (appointed in 1930)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Phú was elected as the first General Secretary of the Communist Party of Vietnam (Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam) after the unification of multiple groups by the Comintern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Phú được bầu làm Tổng Bí thư đầu tiên của Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The first General Secretary of the Communist Party of Vietnam (Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam) elected in 1930."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
